<!--
    kuna analysis (option aif): no gap-walk function starts inside the code of a
    sized PowerPC64 ELFv1 symbol, whose value is a descriptor in .opd.

    Twenty-five leaves open with std 4,-8(1); addis 5,3,1; addi 3,5,n.  The same
    three instructions occur inside sample, which a symbol in .dynsym sizes at 28
    bytes:
        0x1068  cmpdi 3,0 / beq 0x1080 / nop
        0x1074  std 4,-8(1) / addis 5,3,1 / addi 3,5,7
        0x1080  blr
    The size was read as that of the bytes at the descriptor, so the gap walk
    named sub_1074 and sample ended there without its result.  exact24 is the same
    shape in 24 bytes with no .name symbol.

    These keep their starts: the routine behind sample that has no symbol
    (0x1084), inner, a symbol inside outer (0x10a0), the routine behind the 8
    bytes of dotted (0x10d4), whose descriptor symbol states the 24 bytes of its
    descriptor and whose .dotted symbol the 8, as the dot-symbol ABI does, the code
    a descriptor with no symbol names inside local (0x1144), and the target of a
    call from caller, which nothing calls, inside reached (0x1128).

    Stage: P1 program prep (code/data partition), option aif (the drivers' default
    on every architecture but x86-64).  Single pass per byte order.

    Images: decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/
    elfv1_symbol_extent_be.so and elfv1_symbol_extent_le.so
    (elfv1_symbol_extent.S).
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">4e80002000000000</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
